      <h1 id="cluster-api-troubleshooting" class="group scroll-mt-20">Troubleshooting clusters that use the Cluster API<a href="#cluster-api-troubleshooting" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>To help avoid or recover from issues in a cluster that supports migrating resources to use a different authoritative API, you can learn how to recognize these issues. Generally, troubleshooting steps for problems with the Cluster API are similar to those steps for problems with the Machine API.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Managing machines with the Cluster API is a Technology Preview feature only. Technology Preview features are not supported with Red Hat production service level agreements (SLAs) and might not be functionally complete. Red Hat does not recommend using them in production. These features provide early access to upcoming product features, enabling customers to test functionality and provide feedback during the development process.</p>
